unds Containing Nitrogen Question 180 Hindi Option 4\">"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"aliphatic-amines","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-february-morning-slot","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-february-morning-slot","active":true},{"question_id":"NKOpVAGoGWm7IuwX5F1kludvp91","chapter":"alcohols-phenols-and-ethers","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements--brbrstatement-i--o-n-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-5rfscwjfgvgjah3n","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements : <br><br>Statement I : o-Nitrophenol is steam volatile due to intramolecular hydrogen bonding.<br><br>Statement II : o-Nitrophenol has high melting due to hydrogen bonding.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kqv8syis/7552b3e6-dd3d-4bdb-89c5-7e01005a989c/2ea83840-e01a-11eb-8de8-59af26dc1e90/file-1kqv8syit.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 120 English Explanation\">\n<br><br>So it is more vo